{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WxnyiS7wVzkHq7JvKLiSpS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from man pages diverge on edge cases that break scripts and pipelines. This project derives formal specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components:\n- `cmd/` — One Go package per utility, compiled to standalone binary\n- `pkg/sys/` — Darwin/Linux syscall abstractions\n- `pkg/format/` — Shared output formatting (tables, colors, human-readable sizes)\n- `pkg/testutils/` — Differential testing harness (runs Go binary vs GNU reference binary)\n- `magefiles/` — Build targets (excluded from generation scope)\n\n**Current State**: All specifications are complete for releases 00.0 through 01.3. No generated code exists on the working branch — prior generated code (4,586 LOC) lives only at tagged commits from earlier pipeline runs. All use cases in release 00.0 show `codestatus: not started`.\n\n**Current Release**: Release 00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure) with four use cases:\n- `rel00.0-uc001-magefiles` — excluded from generation (DD7)\n- `rel00.0-uc002-format` — code not started\n- `rel00.0-uc003-sys` — code not started\n- `rel00.0-uc004-testutils` — code not started\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 is the earliest incomplete release. Three use cases are eligible for code generation: format, sys, and testutils. All three are independent foundational libraries with no inter-dependencies (pkg/format takes width as a parameter rather than importing pkg/sys). Following P8 deterministic ordering — equal-priority libraries ordered alphabetically by primary file path — `pkg/format/` comes first.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/format -- size formatting, column alignment, ANSI color (rel00.0-uc002-format)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/format component description and design decision DD3 -- shared formatting library)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc002-format.yaml (format package use case)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (release 00.0 test suite covering format acceptance criteria)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (list this directory and read the PRD for pkg/format -- it covers human-readable size formatting, column alignment, and ANSI color output)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/size.go\n        action: create\n        note: Human-readable byte size formatting functions (K/M/G/T suffixes)\n      - path: pkg/format/column.go\n        action: create\n        note: Column alignment and tabular output formatting functions\n      - path: pkg/format/color.go\n        action: create\n        note: ANSI color code constants and colorization functions for file types\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement human-readable byte size formatting per the format PRD: convert byte counts to K, M, G, T suffixed strings matching GNU coreutils --human-readable output conventions\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement column alignment for tabular output per the format PRD: calculate column widths from input data and produce padded, aligned rows suitable for ls -l style display\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement ANSI color output per the format PRD: define color code constants for standard Unix file types (directory, symlink, executable, pipe, socket, block device, char device) and export a function to apply color escapes to strings by file type\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow DD3 from ARCHITECTURE.yaml: common formatting logic lives in pkg/format rather than being duplicated across cmd/ packages. Every cmd/ package that needs formatting imports pkg/format.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"pkg/format is a pure formatting library with no platform-specific dependencies. It does not import pkg/sys. Terminal width and other platform-specific values are passed in by callers, not queried internally.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Human-readable size output must match GNU coreutils conventions so that cmd/ utilities using pkg/format pass differential tests against Homebrew reference binaries (project success criterion SC1).\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/format/size.go compiles and exports a function that formats byte counts as human-readable strings with K/M/G/T suffixes\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"pkg/format/column.go compiles and exports functions for computing column widths and formatting aligned tabular rows\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"pkg/format/color.go compiles and exports ANSI color code constants and a colorization function that wraps strings in escape sequences by file type\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/format/... succeeds with no compilation errors\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/format/... reports no issues\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":34553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":12652,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3cd40da-b7af-418a-8337-08775eeefe54","uuid":"ba004f66-70a1-4375-80b1-000000000001"}
