cmd/ packages. Every cmd/ package that needs formatting imports pkg/format.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"pkg/format is a pure formatting library with no platform-specific dependencies. It does not import pkg/sys. Terminal width and other platform-specific values are passed in by callers, not queried internally.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Human-readable size output must match GNU coreutils conventions so that cmd/ utilities using pkg/format pass differential tests against Homebrew reference binaries (project success criterion SC1).\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/format/size.go compiles and exports a function that formats byte counts as human-readable strings with K/M/G/T suffixes\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"pkg/format/column.go compiles and exports functions for computing column widths and formatting aligned tabular rows\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"pkg/format/color.go compiles and exports ANSI color code constants and a colorization function that wraps strings in escape sequences by file type\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/format/... succeeds with no compilation errors\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/format/... reports no issues\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c3cd40da-b7af-418a-8337-08775eeefe54","total_cost_usd":0,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{},"permission_denials":[],"uuid":"e4d7cef7-5a2d-4412-8bbe-103dc9498b88"}
